# Website Audit Toolkit — secrets template.
#
# HOW TO USE
#   cp .env.example .env   &&   edit .env   (real .env is gitignored — never commit it)
# run-audit.sh auto-loads ./.env and <toolkit-dir>/.env at startup. Real environment
# variables always take precedence over the file.
#
# CLAUDE CODE ON THE WEB
#   Don't put keys in a file in the repo. Set them as environment variables / secrets
#   in your environment configuration (they are injected into the session, not stored
#   in git). See https://code.claude.com/docs/en/claude-code-on-the-web
#
# Presence of each key is reported (value never printed) by run-audit.sh preflight.

# urlscan.io API key — enables the independent external reputation + render vantage
# (Stage 4). Get one at https://urlscan.io/user/profile/ . Without it, Stage 4 is
# skipped and a local browser capture is used instead.
URLSCAN_API_KEY=

# PSI_KEY is intentionally NOT required. The toolkit uses local Lighthouse as the
# standard performance method; set this only if you specifically want PSI/CrUX
# field data. Leaving it empty is the recommended default.
# PSI_KEY=
